# s710_ideas.oot — Idea Fairy 🧚 residual 7.10 HIGH parse-env concat (path-A)
# Date: 2026-08-12
# Role: creative but **shippable** residual ideas — **no product code** this pass
# Audience: Domain Experts (implement winner) · peers (smoke / ident-class) · Memory
# Scope: `c_parse_secret_env` 7.10 close — **same slice-once as 7.1/7.2** — **not** M1–M20, not full IFC

## Problem (tree truth)

| Fact | Evidence |
|------|----------|
| Sprint pin | `SPRINT.oot` 7.10 HIGH: `c_parse_secret_env` **char-by-char leak** |
| 7.1 / 7.2 already closed | Path-A **slice-once-per-span** (`str_slice`, not C `char[]`). 7.1 `c_guard_scan_idents` L105; 7.2 `c_sys_exec_last_arg` L127. Rollups: `s71_phalanx_rollup.oot`, `s72_phalanx_rollup.oot` |
| Wording already settled | `.oo` has **no** C stack `char[]`. Memory: 7.1/7.2 style = **one `str_slice` per span** (`t1_memory.oot` M-SG1/M-SG3). 7.10 is the leftover **ident** concat of that family |
| Walker exists | `ooda/oodac/c_emit_secret.oo` `c_parse_secret_env` L7–82 — line-start `// SECRET:` needle; skip spaces/tabs; then **`name = name + c` per `is_al` char** (L60) |
| Call sites | `c_emit.oo` L78 file-level tags; `check_secret_println_sinks` L135 re-parse. Output: `__sec__name=1` + `__secref__name=1` via `c_env_put` |
| Ident class (honesty) | 7.10 `is_al` is **alnum/`_` including digit-start**. Lexer / 7.1 require **alpha/`_` start**. Do **not** silently import 7.1 start-class |
| Line pressure | `c_emit_secret.oo` ~264 lines (already OVER 256). Winner must **shrink** the name loop, not add a helper in this monofile |
| Leftover concat (not 7.10) | `c_args_strip_cr` L190 `out = out + c` — **8.6 filter**, not a contiguous span. Lexer `try_scan_ident` L28 `id = id + c2` — token stage, all idents |
| Handoff | `s72_ideas.oot` I3 / `s71_ideas.oot` I4 already named this close: `name = str_slice(src, name_start, k)` |
| Existing fixtures | `secret_invalid_empty.oo` (`// SECRET:` no ident); `secret_midline_safe.oo` (mid-line mention); `secret_multi_name_{fail,pass}.oo`; `secret_sink_fail.oo`. Wired in `secret_sink_enforce_smoke.sh` / T2 depth |
| Needle concat is not the leak | `let needle = "// " + "SECRET:"` is two lits once. `__sec__` + name is **once per directive**. Leak is the **per-char name rebuild** |

**Not this wave:** full IFC, `#[Secret]` attr, `${}` (5.8), rewriting `c_args_strip_cr`, rewriting lexer ident, token-stream-only directive parse, C stack buffers, M1–M20.

## Constraints (hard)

1. **Path A only** — kill per-char OoStr on the SECRET **name** span. Not “perfect taint.”
2. **Winner is slice-once** — same mechanism as 7.1/7.2. Do not invent a third close.
3. **Do not greenwash 7.10 from comments.** Close only on **static slice proof + directive smoke**.
4. **Preserve 7.10 ident class.** Digit-start names stay tagged unless a **named** residual changes the class. Shared helper must not smuggle 7.1 `is_start`.
5. **Last-arg / guard scan stay sliced.** Do not retarget 7.1/7.2. Do not apply ident-slice to `c_sys_exec_last_arg` (comma span).
6. **Leftover sites stay residual.** `c_args_strip_cr` and lexer ident are **later**. Folding them into 7.10 FIXED is a lie.
7. **SPRINT “stack buffer” is not implementable in `.oo`.** Same as 7.1/7.2 — do not emit C `char buf[N]`.
8. **Reuse fixtures.** Prefer `secret_invalid_empty` / midline / multi-name / sink-fail + a **small** TMPDIR matrix (s71/s72 smoke shape).
9. **Line pressure** — no new monofile; do not grow `c_emit_secret.oo`. Inline slice is a net shrink.
10. **Fairy writes ideas only** — DE owns land + prove.

## Darwin scorecard (path-A residual)

Axes 0–10 (higher = survives compile cycle). Sum/5 ≈ rank:

| Axis | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Close** | Moves 7.10 HIGH (per-char name concat) |
| **Honest** | Named residual; no “stack buffer shipped”; leftover sites not folded |
| **Smoke** | Cheap pass+fail: empty name refuse, midline no-tag, real name tags, multi-name |
| **Entropy** | Lowers \(S\) (untested 7.10 FIXED, concat copies, ident-class drift) |
| **Ship** | ≤ few lines in one fn + smoke; no new architecture |

**Rule:** losers pruned. 1–2 winners advance to DE this sprint turn.

---

## Ideas evaluated

### I1 — Slice-once the SECRET name (same as 7.1/7.2) ⭐
**Shape:** Keep the existing line-start + needle + space-skip walk. Change **only** name materialization:

1. After WS skip, `name_start = k`.
2. Advance `k` while `is_al` (same 70-line oracle **or** a local loop — **do not change class**).
3. Empty span (`k == name_start`) → same `ERR\tsecret\tinvalid name…` + `process_exit(1)`.
4. `name = str_slice(src, name_start, k)` — **one** slice. Delete `name = name + c`.
5. `c_env_put` of `__sec__` / `__secref__` unchanged (one concat **per directive**, not per char).

No new helper required. Net line **shrink**. SPRINT 7.10 → **FIXED path-A (slice + prove)** only after I2 smoke 0.

**Smoke:** I2 matrix.  
**Darwin:** Close 10 · Honest 10 · Smoke 9 · Entropy 10 · Ship 10 → **avg 9.8**  
**Why winner:** This **is** the 7.1/7.2 close applied to the leftover leak. Tree already proved the pattern (`t1_memory.oot`, s71/s72 rollups). Avoids helper theater and monofile growth.

### I2 — Directive **edge matrix** (7.10 prove rail) ⭐
**Shape:** One small script (`scripts/s710_parse_secret_env_smoke.sh`, s71/s72 TMPDIR shape) **or** a short addendum on `secret_sink_enforce_smoke.sh`. Dual-path `emit-c` / `check` where cheap. Do **not** invent a second product parser.

| Case | Fixture | Expect | Why |
|------|---------|--------|-----|
| Empty name refuse | `secret_invalid_empty.oo` (exists) | REFUSE `ERR\tsecret` | `// SECRET:` + no ident |
| Mid-line no tag | `secret_midline_safe.oo` (exists) | ALLOW | Line-start only (`SECRET_TAINT.oot` §5) |
| Real name tags | `secret_sink_fail.oo` / `secret_eprintln_fail.oo` | REFUSE | Slice must still produce `__sec__x` |
| Multi-name both live | `secret_multi_name_fail.oo` (exists) | REFUSE | Two directives; two slices |
| Multi-name unused | `secret_multi_name_pass.oo` (exists) | ALLOW | Tags exist; sink clean |
| WS after colon | TMPDIR: `// SECRET:   tok` then `println(tok)` | REFUSE | Existing space/tab skip + slice |
| Tab after colon | TMPDIR: `// SECRET:\ttok` | REFUSE | Same skip |
| Underscore / mixed | TMPDIR: `// SECRET: _A1` then `println(_A1)` | REFUSE | `is_al` includes `_` + digit **cont** |
| Digit-start (class honesty) | TMPDIR: `// SECRET: 1abc` then `println(1abc)` **or** named residual | **Keep current** (tag `1abc`) | Do **not** import 7.1 start-class. Lexer would not scan `1abc` as IDENT — name if sink cannot refuse |
| Long name | TMPDIR: `// SECRET:` + ≥256 `_`/`a` then println that ident | REFUSE | Proves slice, not concat bomb. Keep N modest (lex still concats — I6 later) |
| Static 7.10 | grep `c_parse_secret_env` | `str_slice` present; **no** `name = name + c` in this fn |

**Prefer ephemeral TMPDIR** for new WS / class / long-name cases — do not grow fixture theater.

**Darwin:** Close 9 · Honest 10 · Smoke 10 · Entropy 10 · Ship 9 → **avg 9.6** (rails; not a solo product rewrite)  
**Why must-bundle:** Without this, “7.10 FIXED” is comment-greenwash (same as 7.1 I5 / 7.2 I2).

### I3 — Tiny `c_ident_end` / `c_slice_ident_at` helper
**Shape:** One helper **outside** `c_emit_secret.oo` (file already OVER 256), e.g. `c_emit_args.oo` or `c_emit_helpers.oo`:

- `c_ident_end_alnum(src, start) -> Int` — cont = current 7.10 `is_al` (digit-start **allowed**)
- Caller: `name = str_slice(src, name_start, c_ident_end_alnum(src, name_start))`

**Do not** reuse 7.1 `is_start` (alpha/`_` only) without a **second** helper or a start-class flag. 7.1 walker already sliced; optional call-site swap is **not** this OWN.

**Darwin:** Close 7 · Honest 8 · Smoke 7 · Entropy 8 · Ship 6 → **avg 7.2**  
**Why later / optional:** I1 already closes 7.10 without a helper. Helper is DRY for leftover **ident** sites (lexer, skip/struct name loops) — those are **later residual**. Same-wave only if I1+I2 land **and** line budget in a **different** file. Do not grow 264.

### I4 — Also rewrite `c_args_strip_cr` this wave
**Shape:** Replace `out = out + c` in `c_args_strip_cr` (`c_emit_args.oo` L172–194) with some “slice” of keep-spans.

**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 6 · Smoke 3 · Entropy 4 · Ship 3 → **avg 3.8**  
**Why later residual (8.6):** This is a **filter rebuild** (drop bare CR byte 13 and C `\r` escape). Output is **not** one contiguous source span — slice-once **cannot** implement it without a different primitive (span list join, or accept remaining concat of **kept runs**). Adjacent emit (`c_emit_lower.oo` sys_exec rest) still needs the filter. **Not** 7.10. Named in `s72_memory.oot` S72-5 / rollup. Do not fold into 7.10 FIXED.

### I5 — Also rewrite lexer `try_scan_ident` this wave
**Shape:** `token_scan_ident.oo` L18–28 `id = ch` then `id = id + c2` → `str_slice(src, i0, i)`.

**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 8 · Smoke 4 · Entropy 6 · Ship 4 → **avg 5.2**  
**Why later residual:** Real concat, **same pattern**, but **token stage** for every IDENT/keyword in the compiler. Different OWN. 7.10 names are **not** lexed as the directive ident (parser walks source text). `s71_peer2.oot` already attributed long-ident cost here — do not steal that close. Digit-start class **differs** (lexer refuses). After 7.10, this is the next **ident-slice** candidate (with I3 helper + 7.1 start-class).

### I6 — Literal SPRINT: C stack buffer for the name
**Shape:** Lower name walk to C `char buf[N]` / `chs_rt` helper.  
**Darwin:** Close 3 · Honest 1 · Smoke 2 · Entropy 0 · Ship 1 → **avg 1.4 — DISQUALIFIED**  
**Why dies:** Wrong language layer. 7.1/7.2 already rejected this (`t1_memory.oot` H3).

### I7 — Token-stream directive parse (drop source walk)
**Shape:** Tag SECRET names from lexer comments / a new token. Delete `c_parse_secret_env`.

**Darwin:** Close 5 · Honest 5 · Smoke 3 · Entropy 3 · Ship 2 → **avg 3.6**  
**Why later:** Lex strips `//` before secret token walks (`SECRET_TAINT.oot` §5). Line-start rule lives in the **source** walker. Signature / stage change. Does **not** fix 7.10 heap (slice does). Architecture-adjacent.

### I8 — Full AST / IFC / `#[Secret]`
**Shape:** Typed secret attr; no `// SECRET:` string scan.  
**Darwin:** Close 4 · Honest 3 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 0 → **avg 1.6 — REJECT**  
**Why dies:** Moonshot. Out of residual 7.10.

### I9 — Naive `contains` / split on `SECRET:`
**Shape:** `split` / grep names; no line-start / ident class.  
**Darwin:** Close 2 · Honest 0 · Smoke 1 · Entropy 0 · Ship 6 → **avg 1.8 — DISQUALIFIED**  
**Why dies:** Mid-line FP (`secret_midline_safe`). Undoes Path-A directive rule.

### I10 — Doc-only: “7.10 slice later” / SPRINT flip without smoke
**Shape:** Flip SPRINT from comments; leave `name = name + c`.  
**Darwin:** Close 2 · Honest 3 · Smoke 0 · Entropy 1 · Ship 9 → **avg 3.0**  
**Why not alone:** Greenwash. Honesty line **belongs inside I1+I2**.

### I11 — Unify ident class with lexer / 7.1 now
**Shape:** Change 7.10 to alpha/`_` start while slicing.  
**Darwin:** Close 6 · Honest 4 · Smoke 4 · Entropy 3 · Ship 5 → **avg 4.4**  
**Why not this turn:** Behavior change unrelated to heap. Digit-start is rare; I2 must **name** it. Unify later with I3+I5 if product wants lexer-faithful directive names.

